===Etymology===
From {{suffix|dzīvs|nieks|gloss1=alive|lang=lv}}, or perhaps {{suffix|dzīvot|nieks|gloss1=to live|alt1=dzīv(ot)|lang=lv}}. The original meaning of this word was “living person,” “inhabitant” (now {{m|lv|dzīvotājs}}, {{m|lv|iedzīvotājs}}). The modern meaning of “animal” or “living being” first appeared in the 1860s, in writings by [[w:Juris Alunāns|J. Alunāns]], following the model of {{cog|ru|живо́тное}}, and was registered in dictionaries in the 1870s. Formerly other expressions had been used for this meaning (e.g. {{m|lv|[[dzīvs]] [[radījums]]||living creature}}, or also more specific terms like {{m|lv|lops||farm animal}} or {{m|lv|zvērs||beast}}).<ref>{{R:lv:LEV}}</ref>

